WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.490
Picture a Latin American city:
an old plaza with its market,

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.610
and a grand avenue running
out from the center.

3
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.430
Near that center stand some
of the city's richest homes.

4
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.830
Now picture classic models
of North American cities.

5
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.830
There, wealthier households
tend to live toward the edge.

6
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.990
So why do many Latin American cities
have their richest homes near the center?

7
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.050
Dangerous suburbs?

8
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:25.570
Building bans?

9
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.050
In this mission, you'll test
the North American models,

10
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.270
and the galactic city of
freeways and edge cities.

11
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.310
Then you'll compare city
models from Latin America,

12
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.890
Southeast Asia and Africa,
and see what they share.

13
00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.510
Your mission: explain why many Latin
American cities have their richest homes

14
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.710
near the center.
